  "verbalization": "Ergosta-4,24(28)-dien-3-one appears to be a target of multiple dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family members, which in turn are targets of various compounds that ultimately interact with the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14. This suggests a potential pathway where Ergosta-4,24(28)-dien-3-one may influence the proteasome through a series of metabolic intermediates. The shared involvement of the SDR family members and their downstream targets indicates a possible mechanism by which the compound modulates proteasome activity, possibly through metabolic activation or indirect regulation. The evidence supports a link between the compound and the proteasome subunit, though the exact mechanism remains unclear, as the pathways are interconnected and the direct interaction between Ergosta-4,24(28)-dien-3-one and the proteasome subunit is not directly established.",
